\tag{fdip}
\title{Global symmetry of the scalar field}
\date{2026-11-19}

\p{A finite sum can give the same weight to two opposite values while
concentrating almost all its weight near configurations in which
neighboring values agree. How does a measurement at one vertex distinguish
the mean field from the configurations of greatest weight?}

